  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact of the adoption of EU-Health directives on the medical devices market in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project facilitates Ukraine&#x2019;s smooth alignment with European Union (EU) legislation by providing an evidence-based assessment of the impact of EU-Health directives related to medical equipment (EU 2017/745 and EU 2017/746) on the Ukrainian market. The project provides information for decision-making for the adoption of the regulatory framework that safeguard public access to safe and effective medical devices; mitigates financial and administrative risks for the state and producers; and creates a more predictable and transparent environment for businesses to operate and invest in. By reducing regulatory uncertainty and aligning procedures with EU standards, the project will help businesses plan long-term, streamline compliance costs, and expand market opportunities. This, in turn, will accelerate Ukraine&#x2019;s integration into the EU internal market for medical devices while minimising risks of market shortages and increased costs.</narrative>
  </description>
